00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:06.390
Our Summer

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:06.390
Our Summer

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:07.100
Where's that pretty little black-haired human?

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.020
Come out so we can bleed you!

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.580
Ronja! We're going for it!

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.120
Ronja!

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.550
Ronja!

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:33.620
But, we have to...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.460
You have to...

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:14.180
Why are you two soaked?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.470
Have you been swimming?

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:29.030
Yes, we've been having a little swim.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.900
Birk and I.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:33.840
Hey,

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:37.450
aren't you going to come and greet my mother?

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:43.870
You don't greet uninvited guests.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:51.550
My mother taught me that when she was still cradling me in her arms.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.140
It's a pity your mother didn't teach you some manners while she was at it!

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.910
Birk is just tired.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.040
That's why...

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:46.480
You know why I came, right?

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.360
You didn't come to give me bread?

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.570
No.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.700
You'll get bread when you come home.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:10.590
I can never go back to the fort.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:18.640
Well, then Mattis will wind up
 throwing himself into the river.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.080
Would he throw himself into the river for my sake?

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:28.510
Even though he refuses to utter my name?

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:32.380
Not when he's awake.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:34.530
But...

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.870
Every night he cries in his sleep and calls out for you.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.830
How do you know?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.080
You mean he's come back to your bed?

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.760
He's not sleeping with Per anymore?

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.360
No, he's not.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:09:00.390
Skalle-Per couldn't stand having him there any longer.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:04.600
And I could scarcely stand it either.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.640
But...

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:14.020
He has to have someone to hang onto when things get really bad.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.940
You know, Ronja...

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:25.450
It's hard to see someone being so inhumanly tortured.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:32.670
Look, Mother...

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:41.800
If you were a child, and your father denied you so completely

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.720
that he wouldn't even speak your name,

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:51.310
would you still go back to him?

00:09:55.610 --> 00:10:01.950
When he wouldn't even come and ask you himself?

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.430
No.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.410
I wouldn't.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:19.090
He would have to ask me to return himself.

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:23.430
That's for sure.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:28.010
But Mattis will never ask me to come back!

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.340
Ronja, go lay down.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:07.100
I'll just doze off out here until morning, then head home.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:09.410
Nah.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:12.600
I want to sleep by you.

