00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:44.070
Mother...

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.420
What's wrong, Birk?

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:08.380
I'm sitting here feeling pitiful...

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.800
My sister.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.680
Why?

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:22.230
Because it's only when Greedy Falls is calling that you are wholly and completely my sister,

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.860
but not otherwise.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:32.070
When your father calls through his various messengers,

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:34.530
you are not my sister anymore.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:39.910
And when they come, I act like a coward.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.920
So I'm feeling pitiful about that too.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.130
I— I am too!

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.550
But that's how it has to be.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:57.060
I know that.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:03.440
Even so, do you still want to be my brother?

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.190
Yes, that's just it.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:11.820
I am your brother, wholly and completely, always.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:13.570
You know that, right?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:26.420
Do you know why I wanted us to have this summer in peace,

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:31.340
without any interlopers from Mattis' fort?

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:36.220
Why I cannot bear to talk about the winter?

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.560
Yeah, why don't you...

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.350
It's summer now, my sister.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:51.070
This summer is all we have.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:53.280
For you and me, right?

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:01.000
Ronja, you must return to Mattis' castle before winter.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:02.910
What about you?

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:05.670
I'll stay here.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:10.550
I could go and beg my way back into Borka's keep.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.760
But what good would that do?

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:26.060
I'd still be without you.

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:28.650
I wouldn't even be allowed to see you.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.190
You'll freeze to death.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:41.370
Maybe I will. Perhaps not.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:46.420
If the forest gets completely covered in snow like last winter,

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:54.920
I can't come up here and bring bread or furs for you!

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.090
Don't you realize that?

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:57.590
Birk Borkason?!

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:03.890
Then that's how it will have to be.

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:06.100
But, it's summer now...

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:07.600
My sister.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:15.820
Summer or winter, who said I was going back to Mattis' fort?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:18.320
I did.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:21.830
I'm going to bring you to the fort even if I have to drag you.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:27.540
If I freeze to death, I will be the only one.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:31.460
But, it's summer now.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:32.880
I said so, remember?

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:45.470
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:45.470
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.820
We've never gotten this lucky before!

00:16:55.820 --> 00:17:02.070
Yeah, I guessed that they'd all appear at once today.

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:06.790
Now that we know that, let's snatch them all up quickly.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:07.750
Yeah!

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:31.980
Ow!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:32.980
Look at that!

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:44.930
I won't let anything spoil the time we have left.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:59.190
I'm drinking in the summer like the wild bees sucking up nectar.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:08.200
I'm gathering it all up into a big lump of summer.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:09.370
And...

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:14.290
And it will live on, even when it's not summer anymore.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:24.720
Do you know what's is in it?

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.400
Sunrises.

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:32.520
Blueberry bushes covered with berries.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.850
The freckles you have on your arms.

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:38.400
The moonlight over the river in the evening,

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:39.770
and the starry skies.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:44.700
The woods in the noon-day heat when the sun is shining on the firs.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:48.240
The light rain in the evenings.

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:53.160
The squirrels, the foxes, and the hares...

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:56.580
The moose and all the wild horses we know!

00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:01.300
Times when we swam, and times we rode in the woods...

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:04.800
You know that, right?

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.970
You are the master of the summer montage!

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:12.770
Keep it up!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:42.840
The sky was growing clearer and cooler.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:50.340
But they said nothing about it.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:22.840
Ronja!

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:26.340
What's wrong?

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:31.090
Are you afraid of the fog?

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:36.060
Are you worried we'll lose the way back home?

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:49.780
Do you hear that?

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:52.490
It's the Unearthly Ones' singing.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.790
At last, I can hear their song!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:01.790
Have you never heard it before?

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:04.090
No. Never.

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:09.260
They want to lure us down to the underworld.

00:22:09.670 --> 00:22:10.760
Did you know that?

00:22:11.630 --> 00:22:13.800
Yeah, I do.

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:18.310
You're not thinking of following them, right?

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:24.020
I am not that much of a fool.

00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:28.320
But Skalle-Per said...

00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:33.780
What did Skalle-Per say?

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:38.620
Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:53.840
When the Unearthly Ones come up into the forest and sing,

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:56.850
you know autumn has come.

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:08.650
And then it will soon be winter.

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:13.200
Oh, yes indeed.

